# UI Rules

Use the project's centralized design tokens. Do not introduce arbitrary colors. Do not introduce arbitrary spacing values unless necessary. Use reusable UI components.

The UI should feel modern, calm, premium, fitness-focused, minimal, and data-oriented. Avoid an overly aggressive bodybuilding aesthetic.

Interactive controls should have a minimum touch target of approximately 44px.

Every async operation needs a loading state, success handling, and error handling. Every list needs an intentional empty state.

Avoid deeply nested cards. Prioritize mobile usability. Do not create desktop layouts unless specifically requested.

Keep business calculations out of UI components. Workout logging must stay fast with minimal interaction — the user should be able to start a workout within seconds.
